he observed-to-expected ratio is 15.0, with a 95% confidence interval of 7.6 to 31.7. December accounts for 6% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 6% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 4. Contract [1], for 14,990 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The high ratio shows a pattern, but it doesn't prove any contract was improperly awarded. Prices near the limit can reflect market rates or budget constraints. Legitimate reasons may explain the numbers without indicating wrongdoing.\nWhat can be checked: Check if multiple contracts cover the same need. Review awardee A's contracts for repetition. Look at contract [1] to see if the amount was near the limit due to market conditions or budget decisions.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["PnjCRWJr1Gc%2B1TMyIiZmzw%3D%3D","JsHTaSrcJMZ%2FP7lJ7Fu0SA%3D%3D","gWmWJwjJg2sl5NjlNci%2BtA%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}